<!--
/**
 * Copyright © Two.inc All rights reserved.
 * See COPYING.txt for license details.
 *
 * TWO-26616: the product page "Buy with <brand>" button on Hyvä themes.
 * TWO-26659: the product page promo message on Hyvä themes.
 *
 * The base module adds the button block on every theme. Its template wires the
 * click up through RequireJS, which a Hyvä page does not load, so on Hyvä the
 * button rendered and did nothing. This swaps in a template that does the same
 * thing in plain browser JavaScript. The block and its visibility rules (the
 * merchant's product button switch included) stay the base module's.
 *
 * Its placement moves. The base module hangs the button off product.info.main,
 * just after the add-to-cart form, which on Luma is the purchase column. On
 * Hyvä product.info.main is the whole product page, so the same position put
 * the button below the related products and the review form, just above the
 * footer. product.info.additional is the container Hyvä's product-info template
 * renders last in that column, directly beneath its add-to-cart and wish-list
 * rows.
 *
 * The promo message is the base module's block too, left on its template and
 * its own switch, and it hung off the same base position, so it landed at the
 * foot of the page as well. It moves into the same container, with the button
 * directly above it: the order the base module gives the two on Luma, where the
 * message follows the button beneath the add-to-cart controls. Hyvä's
 * product-info column offers no container nearer the price, which shares a row
 * with the add-to-cart button.
 *
 * Magento runs scheduled moves in the order the moved elements were declared,
 * not the order of these move tags, and skips a before or after naming a
 * sibling not yet in the container as a broken reference. The base layout
 * declares the promo first, so the promo moves with no sibling and the button
 * is placed before it. Whichever move runs first, the button ends up above.
 *
 * The button label and the promo text are resized for a Hyvä theme in this
 * module's own product stylesheet, loaded here so it reaches the product page
 * only.
 *
 * The hyva_ prefix makes Hyvä apply this handle on Hyvä themes only, so a Luma
 * storefront keeps the base template and placement of both.
 */
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <head>
        <css src="Two_GatewayHyva::css/product-express.css"/>
    </head>
    <body>
        <referenceBlock name="two.product.express"
                        template="Two_GatewayHyva::product/express-button.phtml"/>
        <move element="two.product.promo" destination="product.info.additional"/>
        <move element="two.product.express" destination="product.info.additional"
              before="two.product.promo"/>
    </body>
</page>
